Rac8 $2 (19... Rab8 $1) 20. Qe2 $1 Rb8 21. g4 $1 Bg6 22. Bg5+ Kf8 23. Bxd8 $18
Rxd8 24. Bd3 c4 25. Bxg6 hxg6 26. Rd2 Rb8 27. Rfd1 Be7 28. c3 {(20 Dec 1963)}
Qc7 {(13 Jan 1964)} 29. Qh2 Qb6+ 30. Kh1 f6 31. Rd7 e5 32. R1d2 Qe3 33. Qf2 $1
Qh6 34. Rxe7 $1 Qxh3+ 35. Kg1 Kxe7 36. Qa7+ {Adjudication (forced mate).
Bannik obviously had other things on his mind as he was a strong master. 
"Sent for adjudication! Begun June 1963, ended about a year later. Some moves
took weeks to arrive - especially when he was losing! In those years, it was
not 'done' to beat Soviet players, and, it seems, it was not done for Soviet
players to resign in lost positions." Source: Bernard Cafferty} 1-0

