1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 Bxb4 5. c3 Ba5 {(Scorebook has this, not
Bc5)} 6. d4 exd4 7. O-O Bb6 8. cxd4 d6 9. Nc3 Bg4 10. Bb5 Kf8 11. Be3 (11. Ba3
$5 {Heyken & Fette}) (11. Bxc6 {Blackburne-Steinitz}) 11... Nge7 (11... Bxf3 {
used to be thought bad} 12. gxf3 {transposes to Morphy-Schulten}) 12. a4 a5 13.
Bc4 {threat Bxf7} Bh5 14. Rc1 $1 {initiative to White says Chandler, but Black
has two possible improvements to investigate} (14. Kh1 Nb4 15. d5 Ng6 $132 {H&F
}) 14... Qd7 (14... h6 $1 {idea Kg8-h7 when it is not easy to see how White
maintains compensation for P (Heyken & Fette)}) (14... Nb4 {Arguello-Medina})
15. Bb5 Qc8 16. Be2 {White has a beautiful position for hjis P (Botterill)} h6
17. d5 Bxe3 18. fxe3 Na7 19. Nd4 Bxe2 20. Qxe2 Qd7 21. Qf2 Ng6 22. Ncb5 Nxb5
23. Nxb5 {The combined pressure on the c- and f-files is the key to White's
plan. "Estrin published this game in a Soviet source (bulletin of Central
Chess Club?)" (BC). Source: BC scoresheets/scorebooks} 1-0

